      "file_path": "src/admin.js",
      "line_number": 11,
      "line_end": 12,
      "title": "User delete route has no admin check",
      "description": "The DELETE /users/:id route omits the requireAdmin middleware that its sibling routes use. The handler deletes the user named in the URL without checking who sent the request. Any caller who can reach the server can delete any user account. A caller can also walk through ids to delete every user. Add requireAdmin to the route, as the GET /users and POST /users/purge routes already do.",
      "suggested_change": "admin.delete(\"/users/:id\", requireAdmin, async (req, res) => {\n  await db.removeUser(req.params.id);",
      "source": "lens:id-enumeration-sequential",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The DELETE /users/:id route omits the requireAdmin middleware that its sibling routes use. The handler deletes the user named in the URL without checking who sent the request.",
      "consequence": "Any caller who can reach the server can delete any user account. A caller can also walk through ids to delete every user.",
      "fix": "Add requireAdmin to the route, as the GET /users and POST /users/purge routes already do."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "file_path": "src/admin.js",
      "line_number": 22,
      "line_end": 25,
      "title": "Purge drops removeUser promises",
      "description": "The purge handler passes an async callback to forEach, so nothing awaits or catches the removeUser promises. db.removeUser throws for an unknown id, and that rejection goes unhandled. One unknown id in a purge request causes an unhandled rejection that crashes the Node process. The response also reports every id as removed before any deletion finishes. Await Promise.allSettled over the removeUser calls. Report the count of calls that succeeded.",
      "suggested_change": "  const results = await Promise.allSettled(ids.map((id) => db.removeUser(id)));\n  res.json({ removed: results.filter((r) => r.status === \"fulfilled\").length });",
      "source": "lens:async-floating-promise",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The purge handler passes an async callback to forEach, so nothing awaits or catches the removeUser promises. db.removeUser throws for an unknown id, and that rejection goes unhandled.",
      "consequence": "One unknown id in a purge request causes an unhandled rejection that crashes the Node process. The response also reports every id as removed before any deletion finishes.",
      "fix": "Await Promise.allSettled over the removeUser calls. Report the count of calls that succeeded."
    },
